<title>USA: Waban holders to convert $106.7 mln debt.</title>
<headline>Waban holders to convert $106.7 mln debt.</headline>
<dateline>NATICK, Mass. 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Waban Inc said holders of $106.7 million of its 6.5 percent convertible subordinated debentures due on July 1, 2002, have opted to convert the debentures into common shares.</p>
<p>The company said that it will issue about 4.3 million shares due to the conversion.</p>
<p>Convertible debentures not converted by 1800 EDT on June 26 will be redeemed on July 7 for $1,029.97 for each principal amount, upon surrender of the debentures, it said.</p>
<p>Waban, a warehouse merchandising company, operates HomeBase and BJ's Wholesale Club.</p>
